{"type":"text","timestamp":1792482698243,"sessionID":"ses_ea7b508cbffeAFd2Bjpn5iYZkt","part":{"id":"prt_1584b5d1d001tGHSA8U3pd80cD","messageID":"msg_1584b519c001Rm3gKYx4YDYOx2","sessionID":"ses_ea7b508cbffeAFd2Bjpn5iYZkt","type":"text","text":"Done. I've written the complete Zephyr RTOS application to `submission/main.c`.\n\nThe application:\n- Gets the I2C bus from devicetree node `i2c0`\n- Verifies the device is ready before use\n- Defines sensor address as `0x68` and WHO_AM_I register as `0x75`\n- Reads one byte using `i2c_reg_read_byte()`\n- Checks for errors and prints appropriate messages\n- Returns 0 on success or a negative error code on failure\n\nAll requirements have been implemented with proper Zephyr I2C API usage and error handling.","time":{"start":1792482696477,"end":1792482698239}}}
